    keys as the sampler path, gym's own init runs (unwrapped/np_random), and the
    MRO is PickTask -> BaseMujocoTask -> Env -> Generic -> ABC. Six new tests in
    test_gym_env_interface.py cover the path, cross-path observation parity, the
    batched rejection and exhaustion. data_generation 122 passed
    (116 baseline + 6 new), component_tests 71 passed / 2 skipped.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * tasks: gymnasium reset() that samples a new episode
    
    reset() takes the gymnasium signature (seed, options) and calls
    super().reset(seed=seed) so np_random is initialized.
    
    A self-configured task samples a new episode on reset; a sampler-built task
    clears task state and leaves the scene alone, which is the data generation
    semantics and is kept exactly. The first reset after construction reuses the
    episode __init__ sampled -- re-sampling it would discard a scene load before
    the caller ever saw it -- unless a seed or options force otherwise. options
    is whitelisted to house_index/force_advance_scene.
    
    close() now closes the sampler only when the task created it, so a
    caller-supplied sampler is never closed underneath the caller.
    
    Four task subclasses overrode reset() with the old zero-arg signature, so
    reset(seed=...) raised TypeError on the concrete classes; widened to forward
    kwargs.
    
    NOT done: routing sampling through a sampler-local RNG. The samplers use the
    global np.random/random for ~70 sampling decisions, so localizing them would
    change every sampled episode and redefine what config.seed reproduces -- a
    behavior change to data generation, which this work is meant to leave alone.
    reset(seed=) therefore calls the existing process-global
    seed_task_sampling(), documented as such at the call site. reset() without a
    seed touches no RNG.
    
