    tests: re-seed task samplers right before sampling (defensive hardening) (#166)
    
    Each affected test's task_sampler fixture constructed the sampler
    (which seeds random/np.random/torch once in __init__) then immediately
    called .reset(). Re-apply task_sampler.seed_task_sampling(task_sampler.
    current_seed) immediately before .reset() in every affected fixture,
    so each test's deterministic sampling is anchored at the moment
    sampling begins rather than depending on exactly what happened earlier
    in __init__.
    
    This is defensive hardening, not a confirmed root-cause fix. It was
    motivated by main's data-generation-curobo-tests failure on
    test_rby1_door_opening.py::test_policy_determinism (introduced in the
    same commit as #165), but investigation ruled out the originally
    suspected mechanism: all these tests set an explicit house_inds, so
    _get_dataset_index_map() (the only thing in __init__'s pre-seed window
    touching asset/scene enumeration) never runs, and molmospaces-resources
    itself has zero random/seed usage anywhere. The strongest actual lead is
    that #165 also bumped molmospaces-resources 0.0.1b4 -> 0.0.2 in the same
    diff -- a 5-month, 9-release gap this pin had never tracked before -- and
    the failing test's golden array is loaded via that package's resource
    manager. However, diffing the package's code between those two tags
    shows no change to existing data-resolution/caching logic (only new
    humans_rocketbox registration and new unrelated downloader scripts), and
    the actual test-data/scene blobs live outside this repo, so the precise
    mechanism isn't confirmed. It may also be genuine GPU/curobo float
    non-determinism (already flagged elsewhere in this suite, e.g. "high GPU
    variance is killing me").
    
